          "heading": false
        },
        {
          "term": "observer experiences",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "The formation and evaporation of a macroscopic black hole is a complex process which certainly leads to a practical loss of information and an increase of thermal entropy. The same is true of almost all macroscopic phenomena. It is exceedingly diﬃcult to keep track of all the degrees of freedom involved when a large block of ice melts or a bomb explodes, but in principle it can be done. According to the standard",
      "extractCut": true
    },
