        },
        {
          "term": "hole region",
          "heading": false
        }
      ],
      "extract": "It is very useful to have a simpliﬁed setting in which to study black hole physics. Callan, Giddings, Harvey and Strominger (CGHS) suggested for this purpose two-dimensional dila- ton gravity coupled to conformal matter [11]. Their model can be exactly solved at the classical level and has solutions which are two-dimensional analogs of black holes. Quantum corrections are much more amenable to study in this theory",
      "extractCut": true
    },
    {
